{% comment %}
Findings Directory Section
Grid display of all published findings with transition filtering
{% endcomment %}

<section class="findings-directory">
  <div class="findings-directory__container">
    
    <h2 class="findings-directory__title">Browse All Findings</h2>

    <div class="findings-directory__filters">
      <button class="findings-directory__filter-button findings-directory__filter-button--active" data-transition="all">
        All Findings
      </button>
      <button class="findings-directory__filter-button" data-transition="sleep-wake">
        Sleep → Wakefulness
      </button>
      <button class="findings-directory__filter-button" data-transition="work-recovery">
        Work → Recovery
      </button>
      <button class="findings-directory__filter-button" data-transition="stimulation-restoration">
        Stimulation → Restoration
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="findings-directory__grid">
      
      <article class="findings-card" data-transition="sleep-wake">
        <div class="findings-card__header">
          <span class="findings-card__number">Finding 003</span>
          <span class="findings-card__transition-badge findings-card__transition-badge--sleep">Sleep → Wakefulness</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="findings-card__title">
          <a href="/blogs/journal/cold-immersion-sympathetic-activation">Cold Immersion Triggers Rapid Sympathetic Nervous System Activation</a>
        </h3>
        <p class="findings-card__excerpt">
          Cold water exposure activates the sympathetic nervous system within 30 seconds. The effect is acute and measurable: increased norepinephrine, elevated heart rate, and thermogenic response.
        </p>
        <div class="findings-card__meta">
          <span class="findings-card__date">Published Feb 2026</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/blogs/journal/cold-immersion-sympathetic-activation" class="findings-card__link">
          Read Finding →
        </a>
      </article>

      <article class="findings-card" data-transition="sleep-wake">
        <div class="findings-card__header">
          <span class="findings-card__number">Finding 002</span>
          <span class="findings-card__transition-badge findings-card__transition-badge--sleep">Sleep → Wakefulness</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="findings-card__title">
          <a href="/blogs/journal/sleep-inertia-and-neurological-stages">Sleep Inertia Persists Until Full Prefrontal Cortex Activation</a>
        </h3>
        <p class="findings-card__excerpt">
          Your brain doesn't wake up all at once. Sleep inertia—the grogginess upon waking—reflects the delayed activation of your prefrontal cortex and executive function systems.
        </p>
        <div class="findings-card__meta">
          <span class="findings-card__date">Published Jan 2026</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/blogs/journal/sleep-inertia-and-neurological-stages" class="findings-card__link">
          Read Finding →
        </a>
      </article>

      <article class="findings-card" data-transition="sleep-wake">
        <div class="findings-card__header">
          <span class="findings-card__number">Finding 001</span>
          <span class="findings-card__transition-badge findings-card__transition-badge--sleep">Sleep → Wakefulness</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="findings-card__title">
          <a href="/blogs/journal/thermogenesis-and-metabolic-priming">Thermogenesis and Metabolic Priming: How Cold Exposure Extends Wakefulness</a>
        </h3>
        <p class="findings-card__excerpt">
          The elevated metabolic state triggered by cold exposure persists for 15–30 minutes post-exposure. During this window, your core temperature remains elevated and your nervous system remains in heightened readiness.
        </p>
        <div class="findings-card__meta">
          <span class="findings-card__date">Published Jan 2026</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/blogs/journal/thermogenesis-and-metabolic-priming" class="findings-card__link">
          Read Finding →
        </a>
      </article>

      <article class="findings-card" data-transition="work-recovery">
        <div class="findings-card__header">
          <span class="findings-card__number">Finding 004</span>
          <span class="findings-card__transition-badge findings-card__transition-badge--work">Work → Recovery</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="findings-card__title">
          <a href="/blogs/journal/parasympathetic-activation-evening">Evening Parasympathetic Activation Requires Sensory Downshift</a>
        </h3>
        <p class="findings-card__excerpt">
          Your parasympathetic nervous system doesn't activate simply by stopping work. It requires active sensory downregulation—reducing light, sound, and cognitive stimulation.
        </p>
        <div class="findings-card__meta">
          <span class="findings-card__date">Published Feb 2026</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/blogs/journal/parasympathetic-activation-evening" class="findings-card__link">
          Read Finding →
        </a>
      </article>

      <article class="findings-card" data-transition="work-recovery">
        <div class="findings-card__header">
          <span class="findings-card__number">Finding 005</span>
          <span class="findings-card__transition-badge findings-card__transition-badge--work">Work → Recovery</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="findings-card__title">
          <a href="/blogs/journal/blue-light-and-melatonin-suppression">Blue Light Suppresses Melatonin Production for Hours</a>
        </h3>
        <p class="findings-card__excerpt">
          Evening screen exposure delays melatonin onset by 1–2 hours. The effect is dose-dependent: brighter screens and longer exposure create longer delays.
        </p>
        <div class="findings-card__meta">
          <span class="findings-card__date">Published Feb 2026</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/blogs/journal/blue-light-and-melatonin-suppression" class="findings-card__link">
          Read Finding →
        </a>
      </article>

      <article class="findings-card" data-transition="stimulation-restoration">
        <div class="findings-card__header">
          <span class="findings-card__number">Finding 006</span>
          <span class="findings-card__transition-badge findings-card__transition-badge--stimulation">Stimulation → Restoration</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="findings-card__title">
          <a href="/blogs/journal/attentional-restoration-theory">Brief Restoration Periods Reset Cognitive Load Capacity</a>
        </h3>
        <p class="findings-card__excerpt">
          Micro-breaks of 5–10 minutes in low-stimulation environments measurably restore focused attention capacity. The effect accumulates throughout the day.
        </p>
        <div class="findings-card__meta">
          <span class="findings-card__date">Published Mar 2026</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/blogs/journal/attentional-restoration-theory" class="findings-card__link">
          Read Finding →
        </a>
      </article>

    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .findings-directory {
    padding: 4rem 2rem;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .findings-directory__container {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .findings-directory__title {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: #1a1a18;
    margin: 0 0 2rem 0;
  }

  .findings-directory__filters {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .findings-directory__filter-button {
    padding: 0.6rem 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(26, 26, 24, 0.2);
    background: #fff;
    color: #1a1a18;
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    border-radius: 4px;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
  }

  .findings-directory__filter-button:hover {
    border-color: #1a1a18;
    background: #faf7f2;
  }

  .findings-directory__filter-button--active {
    background: #1a1a18;
    color: #fff;
    border-color: #1a1a18;
  }

  .findings-directory__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(300px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .findings-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 1.75rem;
    background: #faf7f2;
    border-radius: 4px;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
  }

  .findings-card:hover {
    background: #f5f2ed;
  }

  .findings-card.hidden {
    display: none;
  }

  .findings-card__header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .findings-card__number {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #999;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .findings-card__transition-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.8rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .findings-card__transition-badge--sleep {
    background: #4a90e2;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .findings-card__transition-badge--work {
    background: #f5a623;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .findings-card__transition-badge--stimulation {
    background: #7ed321;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .findings-card__title {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
  }

  .findings-card__title a {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #1a1a18;
    text-decoration: none;
    line-height: 1.4;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .findings-card__title a:hover {
    color: #666;
  }

  .findings-card__excerpt {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #666;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
    flex-grow: 1;
  }

  .findings-card__meta {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: #999;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .findings-card__link {
    color: #1a1a18;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .findings-card__link:hover {
    color: #666;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .findings-directory {
      padding: 3rem 1.5rem;
    }

    .findings-directory__title {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .findings-directory__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .findings-card {
      padding: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
    const filterButtons = document.querySelectorAll('.findings-directory__filter-button');
    const findingsCards = document.querySelectorAll('.findings-card');

    filterButtons.forEach(button => {
      button.addEventListener('click', function() {
        const selectedTransition = this.getAttribute('data-transition');

        filterButtons.forEach(btn => {
          btn.classList.remove('findings-directory__filter-button--active');
        });
        this.classList.add('findings-directory__filter-button--active');

        findingsCards.forEach(card => {
          const cardTransition = card.getAttribute('data-transition');
          if (selectedTransition === 'all' || cardTransition === selectedTransition) {
            card.classList.remove('hidden');
          } else {
            card.classList.add('hidden');
          }
        });
      });
    });
  });
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Findings Directory",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}